<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 37,491 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 37,491 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 37,491 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Tuesday, compared to 65,249 tonnes on in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Tuesday	  Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			 7,170	    9,913</p>
<p>    Import cargo			30,321	   55,336</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, seven ships sailed and three berthed. In the next 24 hours, eight ships were expected to sail and 12 were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		  Berthing</p>
<p>High speed deisel    52,000	 Keefan		5/11</p>
<p>Crude oil		65,000	 Capitan Miranda   5/11</p>
<p>High speed diesel    34,000	 Al-Deerah	    due</p>
<p>Sugar		    14,000	 Gemstar-1	   5/11</p>
<p>Fertilizer	     31,802	 Cargo Explorer    3/11</p>
<p>Fertilizer	     28,995	 Alexandros-P	7/11</p>
<p>Pig Iron		  4,984	 Trunovsk	     due</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
